@startuml
title Step 5 - Deployment State Machine

hide empty description

state "Created / Validating\n(execution only)" as CREATED
state "Rejected / Validation Failed\n(execution only; no persisted row)" as REJECTED
state "Validated / Awaiting Confirmation\n(AWAITING_CONFIRMATION)" as AWAITING_CONFIRMATION
state "Infrastructure Reconciling\n(CONFIRMED)" as CONFIRMED
state "Infrastructure Ready\n(INFRASTRUCTURE_READY)" as INFRASTRUCTURE_READY
state "Configuration Resolved\n(CONFIGURATION_RESOLVED)" as CONFIGURATION_RESOLVED
state "Submitted to CD\n(SUBMITTED)" as SUBMITTED
state "Failed\n(FAILED)" as FAILED

[*] --> CREATED : createDeployment / initialize deployment attempt

CREATED --> AWAITING_CONFIRMATION : validateDeploymentInput [valid] /\nbuildDeploymentGraph; resolveResourceDefinitions;\nplanInfrastructureChanges; persist Deployment
CREATED --> REJECTED : validateDeploymentInput [invalid, A1] /\nreturn validation error; rollback attempt
REJECTED --> [*]

AWAITING_CONFIRMATION --> AWAITING_CONFIRMATION : confirmDeployment [invalid override, A1] /\nreturn validation error; keep AWAITING_CONFIRMATION
AWAITING_CONFIRMATION --> CONFIRMED : confirmDeployment [valid overrides] /\napplyInfrastructureOverrides

CONFIRMED --> INFRASTRUCTURE_READY : reconcileInfrastructure [success] /\npersist create/update/reuse Resource Instances
CONFIRMED --> FAILED : reconcileInfrastructure [failure, A2] /\nsaveDeploymentRecord(failed step, error summary)

INFRASTRUCTURE_READY --> CONFIGURATION_RESOLVED : collectResourceOutputs;\nresolveEnvironmentConfiguration [success]
INFRASTRUCTURE_READY --> FAILED : resolveEnvironmentConfiguration [runtime failure, A2] /\nsaveDeploymentRecord(failed step, error summary)

CONFIGURATION_RESOLVED --> SUBMITTED : generateResolvedApplicationSpecification;\ngenerateKubernetesManifest; adaptManifestForTarget;\nmaterializeEnvironmentConfiguration; materializeSecretConfiguration;\npublishDesiredDeploymentState [accepted] /\nsaveDeploymentRecord(delivery reference, SUBMITTED)
CONFIGURATION_RESOLVED --> FAILED : manifest generation/materialization or\npublishDesiredDeploymentState [failure, A2] /\nsaveDeploymentRecord(failed step, error summary)

SUBMITTED --> [*]
FAILED --> [*]

note right of CREATED
  CREATED is an execution-only attempt state.
  createDeployment() persists a Deployment only after
  successful validation, directly as AWAITING_CONFIRMATION.
end note

note right of REJECTED
  This outcome is not Deployment.status = FAILED.
  Contract 4 A1 rolls back deployment, workload_deployment and
  deployment_context rows; no Deployment Record or Deployment
  Step exists for the rejected attempt.
end note

note right of FAILED
  FAILED is only a persisted post-creation Deployment state.
  For UC-03 A2, Deployment and Deployment Record use FAILED;
  the failed Deployment Step stores errorSummary and
  relatedComponentReference when identifiable.
end note

note bottom of SUBMITTED
  UC-04 progress markers are separate deployment_step rows,
  not mutually exclusive Deployment.status values:
  * Infrastructure Ready
  * Configuration Resolved
  * Manifest Generated
  * CD Synced
  * Application Ready

  Their individual statuses can be displayed simultaneously.
  UC-04 reads/aggregates repository, CD and workload status;
  it does not transition the Deployment aggregate. Under the
  current operation contracts, the aggregate remains SUBMITTED
  after CD acceptance (or FAILED on a contracted A2 path).
end note

@enduml
